{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362614-using-antagonist-rules-for-player-characters","id":1362614,"title":"Using Antagonist Rules for Player Characters","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-22T04:08:34-08:00","id":1362614,"title":"Using Antagonist Rules for Player Characters","content":"I'm planning a prelude/prologue. Essentially just a fight, so we can all learn the rules. The PC's will be human baseline characters, they will afterwards go on to create Psions for the full game. <br /> <br /> So (as has been suggested in my other thread) i'm going to use an NPC template for the PC's rather than create full characters using stats and rules they wont need right away,<br /> <br /> To that end, how do I guage what level of threat = such a character (assume a baseline human in Aeon, no powers/talents, just gear).<br /> <br /> Should I use the Defence listed for the NPC, or set it to 1 as per the regular character creation rules? What about Enhancement? I'd like to keep all this simple for now. Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25906-ghost-whistler","name":"ghost whistler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25906_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T04:23:14-08:00","id":1362615,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m not sure how much effort you\u2019ll save going down this path. You\u2019re essentially going to teach your players how to use rules that apply to NPCs but don\u2019t apply to PCs, then they\u2019ll have to unlearn and relearn everything when you move to using PCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T05:08:30-08:00","id":1362620,"title":"","content":"I'm with Bunyip on this one. Just cobble together some very basic templates for the players to use and go at it that way. Get them familiar with the rules that <i>they'll</i> be using - not the ones you'll be using.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T06:43:49-08:00","id":1362630,"title":"","content":"My suggestion was for replacing a ship crew by a NPC so you get some scale fight and introduce the power of the Aberrants to the players.<br /> <br /> For characters it\u2019s a little too simple, but can be done if the characters are really meaningless.<br /> <br /> My suggestion as a story guide is go for a session 0 with your players so they can create their characters, and tell them the story as they learned thru whatever way. Latter in the game they may learn the details thru a flashback or something.<br /> <br /> Now on your approach:<br /> I suggest you to use the defense rules (not the fixed value) as they learn it the proper way. Use the desperation pool for that roll.<br /> Equipment is always a issue, I would give them an standard military equipment (assault weapon, armor, knife, hand gun, survival gear)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 01-22-2020, 09:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T08:01:19-08:00","id":1362651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362614-using-antagonist-rules-for-player-characters?p=1362620#post1362620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm with Bunyip on this one. Just cobble together some very basic templates for the players to use and go at it that way. Get them familiar with the rules that <i>they'll</i> be using - not the ones you'll be using.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you know where I can find some simple stats? I don't want to go through character creation with them at this point","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25906-ghost-whistler","name":"ghost whistler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25906_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T08:32:27-08:00","id":1362655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/294762/Trinity-Continuum-Aeon-ReadyMade-Characters\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/images/4261/294762.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/294762/Trinity-Continuum-Aeon-ReadyMade-Characters\" target=\"_blank\"> Trinity Continuum: Aeon Ready-Made Characters - Onyx Path Publishing | Trinity Continuum | DriveThruRPG.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/294762/Trinity-Continuum-Aeon-ReadyMade-Characters\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/294762/Trinity-Continuum-Aeon-ReadyMade-Characters </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Trinity Continuum: Aeon Ready-Made Characters - Don&rsquo;t wait, humanity needs you now! Do you want to game but your players aren&rsquo;t sure what to play? Looking for inspi </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T10:38:55-08:00","id":1362677,"title":"","content":"Especially if you are going to be working through chargen after the fact with them, maybe make the characters yourself via standard character creation ahead of time, this way you'll be familiar with some of the idiosyncrasies of the process.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T13:44:05-08:00","id":1362717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362614-using-antagonist-rules-for-player-characters?p=1362630#post1362630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My suggestion was for replacing a ship crew by a NPC so you get some scale fight and introduce the power of the Aberrants to the players.<br /> <br /> For characters it\u2019s a little too simple, but can be done if the characters are really meaningless.<br /> <br /> My suggestion as a story guide is go for a session 0 with your players so they can create their characters, and tell them the story as they learned thru whatever way. Latter in the game they may learn the details thru a flashback or something.<br /> <br /> Now on your approach:<br /> I suggest you to use the defense rules (not the fixed value) as they learn it the proper way. Use the desperation pool for that roll.<br /> Equipment is always a issue, I would give them an standard military equipment (assault weapon, armor, knife, hand gun, survival gear)</div> </div> </div> </div>Figure equipment is going to be a little irrelevant here. The &quot;equipment&quot; will be the big-ass military ships the psuedo-PCs are commanding against the Aberrant and its followers.<br /> <br /> All the OP needs to do is come up with the skills/attributes that the psuedo-PCs (the temporary characters the players will portray in this initial fight). In some ways using the NPC Threat idea would work better but it's also a good idea ti get the players familiar with the system that they'll be using.<br /> <br /> So, go halfway instead. Provide Attributes and applicable skills and/or Edges with the psuedo-PC serving as kind of crew amalgamation of pilot, gunner, engineer, etc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}